{
  "facts": [
    "Content rules in src/rules/contentLimits.ts inspect .slidev-layout roots; custom layouts must supply that class, as documented in README.md.",
    "Character counts include laid-out text even when CSS clips or clamps it; data-slidev-check-ignore is the explicit exclusion mechanism for intentionally excluded content.",
    "Text metrics inspect HTML/SVG light-DOM text; SVG resource definitions, use-instance text, shadow-root text and direct native MathML are outside the documented scope, while Slidev's standard KaTeX HTML rendering is counted and its MathML accessibility copy is excluded.",
    "The guideline's visual ten-line budget requires manual review; automatic content checks cover body characters, list depth, and table rows, alongside the existing layout rules.",
    "Hidden rows and list items are counted through descendants only when supported DOM text passes visibility checks and has measurable text geometry; graphic-only visibility overrides require manual review, while a visible structure box itself still counts, including empty boxes and boxes whose contents are skipped by content-visibility:hidden. Text eligibility does not determine whether a visible structure box counts.",
  ],
}
